  "cves": [
    {
      "id": "CVE-2026-11861",
      "publishedDate": "2026-08-20T10:39:08.025Z",
      "lastModifiedDate": "2026-08-20T10:39:08.025Z",
      "description": "A flaw was found in FreeIPA. When a trust relationship is configured between FreeIPA and Active Directory, Active Directory users can bypass authentication for FreeIPA services, including the portal, SMB server, and LDAP directory. This is possible by impersonating a client name in the Ticket Granting Service (TGS) due to FreeIPA services not verifying Privilege Attribute Certificate (PAC) certificates. This vulnerability could allow an authenticated Active Directory user to escalate their privileges within the FreeIPA domain.",
      "severity": 9.6,
      "fix_suggestion": "📦 受影响组件：Red Hat Red Hat Enterprise Linux 10\n🛠️ 修复建议：\n1. 确认受影响的版本范围（见上方 Affected Products）\n2. 升级到厂商官方发布的最稳定安全版本\n3. 检查官方安全公告获取补丁链接\n4. 如无法立即升级，实施临时缓解措施：\n   - 网络层：WAF 规则 / IPS 签名 / 零信任策略\n   - 主机层：最小化暴露面 / 禁用危险功能 / 输入过滤\n5. 修复后使用 NVD / 厂商 PoC 验证修复有效性",
